# Deploy

GitHub is version control only. Never GitHub Pages, `actions/deploy-pages`, or
`withastro/action`.

**Published** = a visitor can see the change at https://rtikhonov.com

Production is Cloudflare Worker `rtikhonov`. The live app is the **repository
root** (`wrangler.jsonc` here). Edit `src/`. Open PRs into `main`.

## Everyday ship

1. `npm run check`
2. Merge the PR to `main`
3. Cloudflare Workers Builds deploys (`npm run build`, then
   `npx wrangler deploy`). The Worker is already connected to this repo.
4. Cache-bust curl https://rtikhonov.com and confirm the new string

Dashboard settings live in `docs/deploy.md`. Do not invent a hosting-branch
checkout. There is no second Astro app.

## Emergency only

If Builds is not connected or failed:

```bash
npx wrangler whoami
npm run deploy
```

Cloud Agents need `CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN` in Cursor environment secrets
with **Workers Scripts Edit**. If `whoami` works but deploy returns 403 /
code 10000, the token is too weak — ask the owner to fix it. Do not run
`wrangler login` and wait on a localhost OAuth callback.

## Do not

- Fetch `cursor/cloudflare-workers-hosting` or `cd rtikhonov.com/`
- Treat a green GitHub check as published (check the live URL)
- TodoWrite for a clean-tree ship
- Re-run `check:docs` / `astro build` before `npm run deploy` when the tree is clean
- Hard-require `/Users/rtikhonov/Desktop/...`
